   "wikipedia": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Dave_Clark_Five_Return%21",
   "resumo_en": "The Dave Clark Five Return! is the second US studio album by the English rock band the Dave Clark Five. It features the single \"Can't You See That She's Mine\" and covers of \"Rumble\" by Link Wray & His Wray Men, \"On Broadway\" by The Drifters and the Disney song \"Zip-a-Dee-Doo-Dah\".\nAll of the tracks were taken from the DC5's first UK album, A Session with The Dave Clark Five. LP was released in both mono (LN 24104) and electronic stereo (BN 26104) version. The album was produced by Adrian Clark, a pseudonym combining the names of Dave Clark and engineer Adrian Kerridge.",
